 analysis for us and you can also  extend it  with different types of outputs so let's  see  how this actually works okay so  here you get to the code part of it and  if you have the right data set loaded  which is right here  okay you can just click on run and it  will produce an output right here in  the console now what we'll do in the  context of this program  is we'll try to apply this same method  to a variety of different data sets and  play around with the different  settings so that we can improve  upon these basic outputs so for example  here you can see  a 3d plot with the data set  that we analyzed you can also understand  the model  so you can understand how much variance  does each principal component contain so  to really go through  all of these elements we also have a  full course  and that course explains how this method  works  with a lot more technical detail about  every step of the way  so this is a little overview of some of  the activities  and resources that we will leverage to  make this program  effective interactive and enriching  because we will not only have  interactive sessions where we  talk uh and present the theoretical  background of different projects  but you also have independent time to go  through some of the materials  on your own  now for those of you that are new to  bioinformatics  i would like to recommend a different  program for you to get started  so before jumping into data science you  might be thinking  this seems very advanced for me i'm not  ready  to spend a lot of time and learn how to  code from scratch and how to  deal with these big data sets so i  recommend our introduction to  bioinformatics for biologists  a program that will simplify a lot of  the things that we'll talk about  and prepare you for next stages  for those of you that are more advanced  and you already feel like you are  ready to not only learn about these  methods  but actually apply them to a long-term  research project and your objective is  to publish  present a poster work on your master's  thesis  or incorporate bioinformatics in your  phd program  we encourage you to explore the research  fellowship  which is an opportunity to learn about  these methods  in the context of your own independent  research project  we meet once a week and discuss  progress on your project supporting you  with a system from our mentors  interactive community of interns that  are all working on  their projects so you have a way to  collaborate  get feedback from experts and answer any  kind of technical challenges  that you need to overcome  so again thank you for joining today's  webinar  i hope that these resources were  explained  clearly and thank you to bibsa that did  an excellent job  going through the technical details and  the logistics  you'll hear from us again by email we'll  follow up and see if you need any  assistance  with anything that we presented today i  do want to mention that  in all of the resources that we shared  there's  a free level so you don't have to pay  anything  to get started and what i would  recommend  is to get started with our course  on introduction to bioinformatics  so the introduction to bioinformatics is  a course  that provides you with a broad overview  of the way bioinformatics is used in  medical research basic research  agriculture biotechnology  and the pharmaceutical industry and it's  a great introduction to a lot of these  topics  as well as a survey that you can fill  out to let us know  more about you and help us design  a personalized plan for you to be able  to benefit  from the resources that we have so again  you can register here for free  create your profile become a part of our  community  and start learning for free and these  courses  have certificates that you get upon  completion even the free courses do  and you can explore very affordable ways  to continue and expand your knowledge  as you go through now also on this  platform the coding platform  there are a number of free courses here  as well  and there's a variety of different types  of courses here  including getting started with  bioinformatics on how to process  sequences how to deal with sequence  similarity  how to get started with data science and  r and in python  how to deal with genomic data  metagenomic data  and transcriptomic data and this list  will continue to grow as you become a  part of this  program thank you again  and uh thank you mohit uh for presenting  as well as harpreets for presenting  about your research project  we'll be looking forward to seeing all  of you in the program  when it starts on october 12th  thank you everyone thank you ilya thank  you
 

